'''''Centaurea diluta''''', the '''lesser star-thistle''',<ref name=BSBI07>{{BSBI 2007 |accessdate=2014-10-17 }}</ref> '''North African knapweed''',<ref>{{PLANTS|id=CEDI4|taxon=Centaurea diluta|accessdate=13 January 2016}}</ref> or '''pale-flowered centaury''',<ref>{{Cite book |last=Aiton |first=William |url=https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/page/5875020#page/263/mode/1up |title=Hortus Kewensis, or, A Catalogue of the Plants Cultivated in the Royal Botanic Garden at Kew |publisher=George Nicol |year=1789 |volume=3 |location=London |pages=261}}</ref> is a species of ''[[Centaurea]]''.  It is native to southwestern [[Europe]] and northern [[Africa]].

